00:02:59,392 --> 00:03:02,537
available in that WebSocket server for this

73
00:03:02,537 --> 00:03:04,447
connection that was upgraded. Because with

74
00:03:04,463 --> 00:03:06,678
WebSockets, of course, instead of sending

75
00:03:06,790 --> 00:03:08,940
back a response and being done with that

76
00:03:08,940 --> 00:03:12,069
request, you keep the connection open, so to

77
00:03:12,069 --> 00:03:15,038
say. That is the idea behind WebSockets. So

78
00:03:15,054 --> 00:03:17,188
therefore, we move to a different model from

79
00:03:17,236 --> 00:03:20,074
a request-response model to a live

80
00:03:20,170 --> 00:03:21,421
connection model, you could say.

81
00:03:22,014 --> 00:03:24,835
And we do that with Bun by switching to this

82
00:03:24,835 --> 00:03:26,662
WebSocket block here. So

83
00:03:27,223 --> 00:03:30,108
on that configuration object that you pass

84
00:03:30,108 --> 00:03:32,433
to bun serve, on this entire object here,

85
00:03:32,753 --> 00:03:34,212
you have your routes, you have your Avra

