00:03:34,212 --> 00:03:36,536
configuration, you have fetch, and then you

87
00:03:36,536 --> 00:03:37,546
have WebSocket.

88
00:03:38,203 --> 00:03:41,153
And this WebSocket part here will only

89
00:03:41,185 --> 00:03:43,910
become active if you call upgrade in the

90
00:03:43,910 --> 00:03:46,332
fetch function. So if you upgrade a

91
00:03:46,396 --> 00:03:49,061
connection and then this data will be

92
00:03:49,189 --> 00:03:51,276
available in that WebSocket block in there,

93
00:03:51,292 --> 00:03:54,310
because in that WebSocket block we have an

94
00:03:54,566 --> 00:03:56,733
open method which will be called when a

95
00:03:56,733 --> 00:03:58,884
WebSocket connection is opened, which

96
00:03:58,900 --> 00:04:00,874
happens when we upgrade a connection in the

97
00:04:00,923 --> 00:04:01,099
end.

98
00:04:01,966 --> 00:04:04,968
We have a message method here which will

99
00:04:05,016 --> 00:04:07,375
become active whenever a new message is

100
00:04:07,504 --> 00:04:09,992
received in that ongoing WebSocket

101
00:04:09,992 --> 00:04:11,677
connection. And you'll see how to send

102
00:04:11,677 --> 00:04:12,977
messages in just a second.

103
00:04:13,719 --> 00:04:15,718
And we have a close method, which is the

